      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Coronary heart disease is a disease of epidemic proportions in our modern affluent society. Primary prevention by way of a multifrontal programme appears to offer the most effective and logical approcah to combating this disease. Effective implementation of this approach requires patients to undergo a comprehensive assessment. This establishes accurate coronary risk profiles, identifies AT RISK patients, and is the basis for planning a sound intervention programme."},
